#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186362216 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124542 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "84947238-f446-5261-8ecd-ee263f64e04f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Image of a Vector Under a Linear Map Given the Matrix Relative to Two Bases"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4176c859-5854-5080-bf2e-b0f94f0b8361" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361127} {:answer/id #uuid "6cb06e3c-e23d-5e91-bbec-4e481c417779" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -9\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361321} {:answer/id #uuid "7eaadcc6-81a8-5407-bdd2-2c06f604c335" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -8 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361396} {:answer/id #uuid "a69c20d3-4c5a-587d-8103-f2c720627c8d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361584} {:answer/id #uuid "d8ce3e71-5c81-5e9f-a3e1-5fabb47b6eec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -11 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361801}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d8ce3e71-5c81-5e9f-a3e1-5fabb47b6eec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -11 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361801} :answer-field/id #uuid "2eea433c-814e-5e0e-919d-f13b06399a26" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362027}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c64bcdb5-768e-5293-a151-ad4d8fbb8250" :question/math-academy-id "q-97579" :question/problem "$$\n[T]_{B|C}=[\\begin{aligned}9 & -2 \\\\ 1 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nSuppose $B$ and $C$ are bases of the vector spaces $V$ and $W,$ respectively. The matrix $[T]_{B|C}$ of the linear map $T:V\\to W$ relative to these bases, and the coordinates of the vector $x\\in V$ relative to $B$ are shown above. Find $[T(x)]_{C}.$" :question/worked-solution "The coordinates of the image of $x$ under $T$ relative to the basis $C$ can be found as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[T(x)]_{C} & =[T]_{B|C}\\cdot [x]_{B} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}9 & -2 \\\\ 1 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -11 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186362217 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124543 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8725caed-481c-5fbe-a0c4-cffdcb308881" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Image of a Vector Given With Respect to the Standard Basis Under a Linear Map"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "336fb41f-4416-5b90-9963-63b715d894cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361063} {:answer/id #uuid "6b7b5d9e-e2af-5819-9157-eb95f22a5fe9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361315} {:answer/id #uuid "860742e3-e187-5777-a59d-99f7335da169" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361436} {:answer/id #uuid "d4184a13-5037-5335-bef6-cc89b6e2f44f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361788} {:answer/id #uuid "e7c815cc-4d5f-5de4-92b1-bdce9f7a0197" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361873}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e7c815cc-4d5f-5de4-92b1-bdce9f7a0197" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361873} :answer-field/id #uuid "3e0a7bfb-89f3-51f0-b3f7-efaec681dd46" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362037}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "29ca0842-b657-584e-9ec2-fc1fbb7af353" :question/math-academy-id "q-97584" :question/problem "$$\nB={[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]},\\,[T]_{B|C}=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the basis $B$ of ${R}^{2}$ (shown above) and a basis $C$ of ${R}^{3}.$\nThe matrix $[T]_{B|C}$ of the linear map $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{3}$ relative to these bases, and the vector $x\\in {R}^{2},$ are also given. Find $[T(x)]_{C}.$" :question/worked-solution "We can find the coordinates of the image of $x$ under $T$ relative to the basis $C$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[T(x)]_{C} & =[T]_{B|C}\\cdot [x]_{B}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to find $[x]_{B},$ the coordinates of $x$ relative to $B.$ So, let\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]={x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThis gives us the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-{x}_{1}=-4 \\\\ -2{x}_{1}+5{x}_{2}=-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now row-reduce the corresponding augmented matrix using Gaussian elimination, as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 & -4 \\\\ -2 & 5 & -3\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{1}:=(-1){R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 4 \\\\ -2 & 5 & -3\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 5\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:=\\frac{1}{5}{R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$\n\nFinally, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[T(x)]_{C} & =[T]_{B|C}\\cdot [x]_{B} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
